      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so my flight from LHR to singapore just got cancelled. im stuck at heathrow right now and need to get to sin asap. can u help me figure out what i should look for in new flights so i dont spend like 30 hours traveling? what should i prioritize?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Prioritize non-stop flights first—Singapore Airlines and British Airways both fly LHR–SIN direct, and that’s your best bet to avoid a 30-hour slog. Look for departures within the next 6–12 hours, even if they’re on a different airline or from a nearby airport like Gatwick. Check if your original carrier can rebook you onto a partner airline, and ask about lounge access or meal vouchers while you wait—those are your rights under UK/EU261 if the cancellation is airline-caused. Also, filter for flights with a single connection max, ideally through hubs like Dubai, Doha, or Frankfurt, and avoid anything with a layover longer than 3–4 hours.",
      "source": "target",
